How can I use Java code to search for a specific phrase within a directory and its subdirectories, while also excluding certain file types such as .pdf and .docx?
You can use the following Java code:
import java.io.File;
import java.io.FileNotFoundException;
import java.util.Scanner;
public class SearchFiles {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    File directory = new File("path/to/directory");
    String searchPhrase = "search phrase";
    String[] excludedExtensions = {".pdf", ".docx"};
    search(directory, searchPhrase, excludedExtensions);
  }
  public static void search(File directory, String searchPhrase, String[] excludedExtensions) {
    if (!directory.isDirectory()) {
      return;
    }
    for (File file : directory.listFiles()) {
      if (file.isDirectory()) {
        search(file, searchPhrase, excludedExtensions);
      } else {
        boolean excluded = false;
        for (String extension : excludedExtensions) {
          if (file.getName().endsWith(extension)) {
            excluded = true;
            break;
          }
        }
        if (!excluded) {
          try {
            Scanner scanner = new Scanner(file);
            while (scanner.hasNextLine()) {
              String line = scanner.nextLine();
              if (line.contains(searchPhrase)) {
                System.out.println(file.getAbsolutePath() + ": " + line);
                break;
              }
            }
            scanner.close();
          } catch (FileNotFoundException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
Replace "path/to/directory" with the actual path to your directory, "search phrase" with the phrase you want to search for, and {".pdf", ".docx"} with an array of the extensions you want to exclude.

