```
This command first selects the `temperature_data` array using the `|` operator, then filters out any objects where the `temperature` value is null using the `map(select())` function. It then calculates the standard deviation of the `temperature` values using the `sqrt`, `add`, `length`, and `map()` functions, and stores the result in a new object with the key `standard_deviation`.
