How can I implement a binary search algorithm in Java to find a specific element in a sorted array?
Here is an example Java code to perform binary search on a sorted array:
public class BinarySearch {
   public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int key) {
      int start = 0;
      int end = arr.length - 1;

      while (start <= end) {
         int mid = (start + end) / 2;
         if (arr[mid] == key) {
            return mid;
         } else if (arr[mid] < key) {
            start = mid + 1;
         } else {
            end = mid - 1;
         }
      }
      return -1;
   }

   public static void main(String[] args) {
      int[] arr = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10};
      int key = 8;
      int index = binarySearch(arr, key);
      if (index != -1) {
         System.out.println("Element found at index " + index);
      } else {
         System.out.println("Element not found");
      }
   }
}
You can modify the code to fit your specific array and element to search for.

