import java.util.Arrays;
public class MedianCalculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] numbers = { 8, 21, 10, 5, 9 };
        Arrays.sort(numbers);
        System.out.println("Sorted Array: " + Arrays.toString(numbers));
        int n = numbers.length;
        double median;
        if (n % 2 == 0) {
            median = (numbers[n/2] + numbers[n/2 - 1]) / 2.0;
        } else {
            median = numbers[n/2];
        }
        System.out.println("Median: " + median);
    }
}
```
The program first sorts the given set of numbers using the `Arrays.sort()` method. It then calculates the median using a conditional statement to check if the number of elements is even or odd. If the number of elements is even, it takes the average of the two middle numbers. Finally, it prints the sorted array of numbers and the calculated median. 
