      chart.data.datasets[0].data = data.results;
      chart.update();
    });
});
```
In this example, we first fetch the poll data from the API endpoint using the `fetch` function and then create a new chart using Chart.js. We also add event listeners to the poll form and filter dropdowns to allow users to submit their own responses and filter the data by location or age.
When a user submits a new response, we make a POST request to the API endpoint and update the chart with the new data. Similarly, when a user applies a filter, we make a new request to the API endpoint with the filter parameters and update the chart with the new data.

