To analyze the performances of actors who have portrayed Shakespearean characters, you can start by collecting data on the following:
1. The plays they were in
2. The characters they played
3. Their critical reception
Once you have this data, you can use Java code to analyze it and draw conclusions about the actors' performances. Here is an example Java code that can help you get started:
```
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;
public class ShakespeareanActorPerformanceAnalyzer {

    private Map<String, Integer> playCountMap = new HashMap<>();
    private Map<String, Integer> characterCountMap = new HashMap<>();
    private Map<String, Double> criticalReceptionMap = new HashMap<>();

    public void analyzePerformance(String[] plays, String[] characters, double[] criticalReception) {
        for (int i = 0; i < plays.length; i++) {
            String play = plays[i];
            String character = characters[i];
            double reception = criticalReception[i];

            // Update play count
            if (playCountMap.containsKey(play)) {
                playCountMap.put(play, playCountMap.get(play) + 1);
            } else {
                playCountMap.put(play, 1);
            }

            // Update character count
            if (characterCountMap.containsKey(character)) {
                characterCountMap.put(character, characterCountMap.get(character) + 1);
            } else {
                characterCountMap.put(character, 1);
            }

            // Update critical reception
            if (criticalReceptionMap.containsKey(character)) {
                double currentReception = criticalReceptionMap.get(character);
                criticalReceptionMap.put(character, (currentReception + reception) / 2);
            } else {
                criticalReceptionMap.put(character, reception);
            }
        }
    }

    public int getPlayCount(String play) {
        return playCountMap.getOrDefault(play, 0);
    }

    public int getCharacterCount(String character) {
        return characterCountMap.getOrDefault(character, 0);
    }

    public double getCriticalReception(String character) {
        return criticalReceptionMap.getOrDefault(character, 0.0);
    }
}
```
In this code, we have defined a class called `ShakespeareanActorPerformanceAnalyzer` that contains three maps to store the play count, character count, and critical reception data. The `analyzePerformance` method takes in arrays of plays, characters, and critical reception data, and updates the maps accordingly. The `getPlayCount`, `getCharacterCount`, and `getCriticalReception` methods can be used to retrieve the data for a specific play, character, or critical reception.
